error[L0704]: `text` cannot be replaced here, where a newer text may sit above it
  --> tests/check/text_roots.lym:18:5
   |
15 |     variable string mine = "{depth}"
   |                     ---- `text` can be an earlier call's `mine`, and this `mine` sits above it
...
18 |     text = "{text}x"
   |     ^^^^ replaces `text`
   |
help: only the newest text on a data stack can change; change `text` before `mine` is declared, or after the block that declares it ends

error[L0703]: `text` cannot be replaced while `shown`, a view of it, is still used
  --> tests/check/text_roots.lym:27:5
   |
26 |     constant shown = bytes(text)
   |              ----- `shown` shows `text`
27 |     text = "zz{2}"
   |     ^^^^ this frees the text `shown` shows
   |
help: finish with `shown` before `text` changes, or copy the text first with `constant kept = text`, and show `kept`

